-- title:
--   Reduction at ℓ∤ N preserves integrality over ℚ̄[j]
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` such that $\ell$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`). Let $y$ be a formal Laurent series with coefficients in $A$, i.e. an element of `LaurentSeries A`. Two hypotheses are imposed on $y$. First, its image $x$ under the coefficientwise ring map `coeffMap A.subtype` induced by the inclusion $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by `divisorExpansions N`. Second, $x$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}=q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24})$ of the modular invariant. The conclusion is that the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (IsLocalRing.residue A) y` of $y$ to the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ is integral over the $k_A$-subalgebra of $k_A((q))$ generated by `jqModC k_A`, the series $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $k_A$ of the integral power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$.
--
--   This is the good-reduction statement for the $j$-chart of the modular function field of level $N$ at a prime $\ell\nmid N$, in the style of Deuring's reduction theory of function fields and Igusa's Kroneckerian model: integrality over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j]$ of an $A$-integral $q$-expansion descends to integrality over $k_A[\bar\jmath]$ after coefficientwise reduction. It is used, together with its companion for the chart at $j^{-1}$, in the construction of mod $p$ modular forms from $q$-expansions.
-- source:
